WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.030
Ostentatious, exaggerated, colossal.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:07.899
It seems that Dubai always aspires to carry
out the largest, most luxurious and most eccentric

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:16.100
projects in the world.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.930
In this small territory we can find the tallest
building, the most luxurious hotel, and even

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.119
the largest international airport on the planet.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:27.480
Located in a strategic enclave at the mouth
of the Persian Gulf, the growth process of

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.730
Dubai is one of the fastest in human history.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.060
In just over 20 years it has gone from being
a remote and lost enclave in the desert to

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.040
becoming one of the world's great capitals.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.761
In this period of time the emirate of Dubai
has multiplied by four its population, by

00:00:40.761 --> 00:00:45.900
nine the number of visitors, and by eight
the size of its economy,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.710
But ... Having said that, the question is:
how has all this development been achieved?

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.900
Has it all been just a matter of oil?

00:00:53.900 --> 00:01:06.000
Well in this VisualPolitk video we’re going
to talking all about Dubai.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.120
Dubai is one of the seven emirates that make
up the United Arab Emirates.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.870
We could describe its government as an Islamic
autocracy that restricts a large part of its

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.080
peoples civil liberties.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.280
However, if we compare it with its neighboring
countries, Dubai is by far the most open place

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.020
in the Middle East.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.980
Want some examples?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.690
Well, here women can drive, the veil is not
mandatory, you can buy pork at the supermarket,

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.700
and even alcohol is not hard to come by.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.960
Yes... things are starting to change, and
in a way I think we could refer to this city

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.730
as a kind of oasis in the middle of the desert.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:50.360
And, as you can imagine, all of this change
has had its reward.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.370
And, well, it might just suprise you…

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.760
Did you know that Dubai is already the fourth
most visited city in the world (when it comes

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.479
to international visitors) and that it surpasses
epicenters of tourism and global trade such

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:05.190
as New York, Hong Kong or Singapore?!

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:11.319
Well it totally is, and this is something
that surprises a lot of people!

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:15.860
Of course, there’s one thing we have to
be clear on here, Dubai does not aspire to

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:25.110
be the freest place on earth, but they do
want to become the richest.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.560
Examples of opulence in this place are so
evident that it is not strange to see the

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:35.650
Dubais police patrol the streets in Ferraris
or Lamborghinis...

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.731
Where else in the world could you possibly
see something like this?!

00:02:38.731 --> 00:02:45.220
Maybe at this moment some of you are thinking
that all this exuberance has a very easy explanation:

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.220
oil.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.540
Could it be that Dubai is nothing more than
a dream of sheikhs that’s financed with

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.540
petrodollars?

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.020
Well, although we can not deny the influence
of black gold, the truth is that the real

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.040
key is very different.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.700
The great secret of Dubai is not oil, but
its commitment to trade.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.700
Don't believe me?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:10.390
Well, let’s dive a little deeper…

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:16.900
NOT ENOUGH OIL
At the end of the 1950s, important oil deposits

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.130
were discovered in the vicinity of Abu Dhabi,
the capital of the Emirates.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:28.280
Be careful here, because we are not talking
about a small discovery, but an a about a

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.280
huge amount of oil.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.790
To give you an idea, it is estimated that
the oil wealth of the Emirates - their proven

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.370
reserves - is even greater than those of all
Russia.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:40.100
However, in the case of Dubai it was a bit
different...

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.030
It is true that this territory was also graced
with the fortune of black gold ... But its

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.300
authorities soon realized that their reserves
were much smaller than those of their compatriots

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.430
in Abu Dhabi.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:57.530
In fact, although it may surprise us, oil
today accounts for less than 1 in every 100

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.769
dollars produced by Dubai’s economy...

00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:03.480
You’ve probably heard about how important
it is to diversify an economy, right?

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:09.530
Well, that is precisely what Dubai did: overcome
dependence and addiction to oil.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.660
Now this is very easy to say, but ... The
question is:

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.660
How did they do it?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:18.900
What did Dubai do to achieve such development
and achieve a higher standard of living even

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.100
compared to its oil-rich neighbors?

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:30.710
Basically, what it did was attract multinationals
and professionals from all around the world.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.650
To achieve this, the first thing they did
was to bet on a low tax policy.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.539
Look, in Dubai they do not have income tax;
the tax on profits is practically non-existent

00:04:39.539 --> 00:04:43.879
and currently purchases are not taxed either
- although the latter is about to change.

00:04:43.879 --> 00:04:47.550
As a result of a joint agreement of all the
member countries of the Persian Gulf Cooperation

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.360
Council, a tax on purchases will soon be launched.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.979
However, the rate will be around 5%, far from
the rates of more than 18% so common in developed

00:04:54.979 --> 00:04:58.990
countries.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:07.620
And, of course, in case you are wondering,
in Dubai there are no taxes on gasoline either.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.620
Yes I know.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.370
It almost seems like we are talking about
another planet…

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:16.099
But do not think that low taxes are the only
strategy Dubai has followed, not at all…

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:20.219
Second, and perhaps even more important than
taxes, Dubai has resorted to an instrument

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:25.270
known as "Special Economic Zones," although
here they are somewhat different from what

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.789
we can find elsewhere.

00:05:26.789 --> 00:05:31.099
In Dubai, these special areas, in addition
to having tax benefits, even have their own

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:36.800
regulations - almost laws - which, as you
can imagine, are always focused on promoting

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.819
business activity.

00:05:37.819 --> 00:05:42.509
Precisely, thanks to having specific rules,
companies can escape the rigidity of legal

00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:47.621
systems that are inspired by sharia law; something
that applies, of course in the rest of the

00:05:47.621 --> 00:05:52.240
emirates…

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:57.240
We can find a good example of this model in
the so-called "Dubai International Financial

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.620
Center", which is almost a state within another
state.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:05.939
Look, this Financial Center has its own judicial
system - chaired by the way, by a British

00:06:05.939 --> 00:06:11.490
judge; with its own official language, which
is not Arabic but English; and has even replaced

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.919
the local currency with the US dollar…

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:18.469
In this way a financial institution, a bank
for example, can do business as if it were

00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:22.469
in Manhattan but benefiting from the tax advantages
of Dubai.

00:06:22.469 --> 00:06:26.120
Not a bad deal, right?

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:32.550
So, now we can understand how Dubai has managed
to attract the most of the 25 largest banks

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:33.550
in the world.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:34.830
But ... This is not all.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:39.990
Along with low taxes and Special Economic
Zones, Dubai also opted for a very high degree

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.449
of immigration freedom.

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:42.889
The result?

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:46.899
96% of its inhabitants have been born abroad.

00:06:46.899 --> 00:06:52.659
But wait, because there's more...

00:06:52.659 --> 00:06:56.210
To further boost foreign investment, at the
beginning of this century the Dubai authorities

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:05.039
made an unprecedented decision for this corner
of the world.

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:11.309
BREAKING MOLDS
In 2002 the government of Dubai approved a

00:07:11.309 --> 00:07:16.229
risky decree that allowed any foreigner, regardless
of their religion, to make real estate investments.

00:07:16.229 --> 00:07:25.069
At that moment the authentic boom began.

00:07:25.069 --> 00:07:29.839
Dubai was full of buildings and large projects:
hundreds of skyscrapers, gigantic shopping

00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:32.529
centers and even the famous artificial islands.

00:07:32.529 --> 00:07:35.259
Now the demand for Dubai become global.

00:07:35.259 --> 00:07:40.979
It’s a fact that since 2002, Dubai has experienced
real estate development comparable only to

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:46.479
that of Shanghai, a city with 13 times more
inhabitants.

00:07:46.479 --> 00:07:53.169
Because another one of the most surprising
things about Dubai is that it has less than

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:54.360
3 million inhabitants…

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.449
Despite this, where before there were only
a handful of skyscrapers, thanks to this decree

00:07:58.449 --> 00:08:03.939
there are now hundreds and huge projects are
announced one after the other... be it new

00:08:03.939 --> 00:08:06.469
skyscrapers, ferris wheels or theme parks.

00:08:06.469 --> 00:08:10.610
One of these latest projects, by the way,
is known as "The Mall of the World", a gigantic

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:15.089
space destined to become the largest shopping
center in the world, and which will even house

00:08:15.089 --> 00:08:20.459
its own cultural district with dozens of theaters
and cinemas, one hundred hotels, and the largest

00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:22.409
indoor theme park in the world.

00:08:22.409 --> 00:08:32.490
The project has been presented as the world’s
first city with a temperature controlled environment!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:41.849
Well, all these measures have made Dubai a
place where it is easy to do business and

00:08:41.849 --> 00:08:47.290
have turned this emirate into a commercial,
touristic, financial, logistical, and even

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.400
industrial power.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:53.160
Yes, anyone who thinks that all this Dubai
thing is only about banks and hotels is very

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.160
wrong…

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.910
Nowadays, Dubai, thanks largely to its modern
ports and special zones, is the third largest

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:05.590
re-exporting power in the world and its industrial
production exceeds 50 billion dollars each

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:07.110
year..

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:15.050
This is what explains why its neighbors are
uneasily watching any fall in the price of

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.890
oil, while the government of Dubai continues
to carry out large projects.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:22.510
It is true, from a strictly political point
of view there are still many reprehensible

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.890
elements when it comes to its religious, social
or human rights issues.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:30.070
There are, for example, the painful conditions
suffered by many construction workers from

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:32.890
countries such as India, Bangladesh or Pakistan.

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:36.890
Of course we can not ignore this reality,
but we can not not paying attention to the

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.870
achievements of this emirate.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:42.460
Among other things because thanks to this,
Dubai has managed to influence the policies

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:46.210
its neighbors are implementing and encouraging
them to reduce their dependence on oil.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:50.340
Dubai is, quite simply, a great model.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:56.630
There is, for example, the new Saudi Arabia
of Mohammed Bin Salman, of which we have already

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.490
spoken about in a previous video.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:03.270
Anyway, I think this case puts a very important
question on the table: Is it possible to reconcile

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:07.830
the absence of civil rights with sustainable
economic growth over time?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.770
History and empirical evidence seem to show
that it is not the situation, but in a world

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:17.890
increasingly pressured by very high taxes
and regulations of all kinds, Dubai’s authorities

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:21.780
seem intent on demonstrating that this time
it will be possible.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.280
At the moment, its commitment to free trade
and investment, and its policies aimed at

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:29.600
strengthening legal security, ease of doing
business and keeping taxes low, have been

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.600
superlative.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.390
If anything, Dubai shows us that competitiveness
and trade tend to have better results in terms

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:36.890
of development than protectionism or subsidies.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:41.480
Many rulers should pay attention to the successes
of this oasis in the desert.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.830
But having said that, now its your turn.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.760
Do you think the Dubai model will make the
Middle East a freer place?

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:51.411
Leave your answer in the comments below as
well as in the survey.

00:10:51.411 --> 00:10:55.720
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

